{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ZHabiroRing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ZHabiroRing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.cyclotomicProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.cyclotomicProjection","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L64-L72","doc":"The cyclotomic projection π_n^{(z)}: ZHabiroElement → Polynomial ℝ /\n(P_n(q, z)) at parameter q. Truncates a Habiro element to its\nrepresentative at level n; together with the compatibility data\nthese are the structural truncations replacing Yekutieli's ad-hoc\ncutoff. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.embedQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.embedQ","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L56-L62","doc":"The constant inclusion ℤ[q^±1] ↪ ZHabiroElement: a function of q\nalone embeds with z-degree 0 (a constant polynomial in z). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement.compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement.compatible","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Compatibility: agrees at level n with level n+1 modulo P_n(q, z). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement.family","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement.family","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Polynomial representative at each level: a polynomial in z (over ℝ)\nwhose coefficients depend on q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroElement","kind":"structure","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L44-L54","doc":"The z-Habiro ring as a compatible family of polynomial representatives\nat each cyclotomic-in-z level. The polynomial structure lets us speak\nof degree, leading coefficient, and unique-representative-of-degree-<n\ninside each quotient. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:z-habiro-ring","label":"def:z-habiro-ring","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.ZHabiroEquiv","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L37-L42","doc":"Equivalence relation on polynomials in z (with q as a parameter):\nf ≡ g (mod P_n(q, z)) iff (f - g) lies in the ideal generated by\nP_n(q, ·). The `Polynomial`-based formulation captures the\npolynomial-degree structure required for the Habiro completion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.zPochhammer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.zPochhammer","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-habiro-ring.lean#L28-L35","doc":"The z-Pochhammer polynomial P_n(q, z) = ∏_{k=1}^{n}(1 - q^{-k} z),\nviewed as a polynomial in z whose coefficients are functions of q.\nUsing `Polynomial ℝ` (with q as a parameter) preserves degree and\nunique-representative structure that the inverse-limit Habiro\nconstruction depends on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}